{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c7901b6231255300","type":"text","text":"# Treasures\n- 15 Sheep and 5 Goats\n- 25 GP per Player\n- Axe of Snaggle Tooth: 2d4+2 Slashing(2 handed, Req 2 STR)\n- Caustic Brew (Heals 3d6+6 HP, but grants the poisoned condition for 3 rounds)","x":0,"y":60,"width":250,"height":297},
		{"id":"af14f610c648ae63","type":"text","text":"# Fight 2 (Sheep Pens)\n1. Kobold Clanger\n2. Kobold Flunkies x6\n3. Kobold Minions (# of PCs-2) x 2","x":520,"y":122,"width":250,"height":198},
		{"id":"cd70469780f04688","type":"text","text":"# Boss Battle\n1. Snaggel Tooth\n2. Kobold Minions x4","x":520,"y":600,"width":250,"height":120},
		{"id":"20c6c1ea4076540d","type":"text","text":"# What's Going on\nThe Small Farming Community of [[Clackston]] in the [[World/Locations/Verdant Strand|Verdant Strand]] is being looted.\n\n- Live stock (Sheep and Goats) are missing.\n- Grain storerooms have been looted.\n- Winter is not looking so bright for the community if they can't get this pillaging under control.\n- Harvest is done and they don't know if they can replenish what was lost.\n- You are a member of a Pose that has been formed in order to find and eliminate the threat to this town's well being.","x":-640,"y":-500,"width":520,"height":420},
		{"id":"9a828abd4345c015","type":"text","text":"# Fight 3\n1. Kobold Den Warden\n\t1. Kobolds x3\n2. Kobold Trapper\n\t1. Kobold Minions X4\n3. Kobold Sneak x2","x":520,"y":357,"width":250,"height":200},
		{"id":"6eab97befdbc41ed","type":"text","text":"# Encounters:\n- [ ] 1 Skill Challenge\n- [ ] 2 Easy Fights\n- [ ] 1 Medium fight\n- [ ] 1 Puzzel\n- [ ] 1 Boss Battle","x":270,"y":-142,"width":250,"height":202},
		{"id":"5fcae6813d0d5a88","type":"text","text":"# Tunnel\n>There is a tunnel to the northwest that appears to go into a finished stone worked tunnel.\n>As you travel further up and further in, you see similar markings on the walls as before. The chamber smells fainty sour and you see patches of moss and some animal bones strewn accross the floor. There is a T in the tunnel. One goes West the other goes North. What do you do?\n\n## Temple Motifs\n>You see a lot of sun imagery and references to a military group that appears to be fighting the shadow or other people would wield weapons of shadow.","x":1680,"y":-1160,"width":360,"height":520},
		{"id":"2aceadbc5ef18425","type":"text","text":"# Sheep Pens (Easy Fight 2 Dun Vol 2 pg 6, Dun Vol 1 pgs 9 & 10)\n\n>You Travel down the tunnel following the sounds of Bleating. As you travel the corridor gradually widens until it is close to 20 Feet wide and opens into a Long room with pillars supporting the ceiling and 2 small rooms at the far end. You don't see the livestock, but it does appear that there is a L at the far end of the corridor that the animal sounds are coming from.\n\n## Encounter\n1. Kobold Clanger in room closest to sheep pen.\n2. Kobold Flunkies x6 Trying to Wrangle sheep in pen\n3. Kobold Minions (# of PCs-2) x 2 Hanging around near the enterence.\n## Treasure\n- [ ] 2 puzzle pieces that the Clanger was using for it's noise.\n- [ ] Caustic Brew x3 (Heals 3d6 HP, but grants the poisoned condition for 3 rounds)\n","x":2090,"y":-1600,"width":405,"height":540},
		{"id":"570d1dd6fccd7e9c","type":"text","text":"# Graffiti\n>Appears to be describing a \"Great Leader\"\n>You also notice the proportions seem to be off of in the graffiti showing some Kobolds that are double the size of others.\n>They are performing terrible acts of pillage and burning of a town that looks an awful lot like **Clackston**\n","x":1040,"y":-1060,"width":300,"height":320},
		{"id":"278a9f2226b9aab5","type":"text","text":"# Fight 1 (Enterence Dun Vol 1 & 2 pgs 29 & 30 )\n> graffiti on the walls. mad with some sort or etching tool or paint.\n\n>Rough hewn stone, not looking like man made Tunnel at all.\n\n>You see many child sized creatures covered in red scales and look to be a cross between a anthropamorphic dragon and crockodile. They see you walk in and immediately scurry towards you with Knives and slings in hand. \"Kill, Kill, Kill\" they cry, \"His ascension is not yet!\"\n>\n **Kobold Minions 3x # of Players**\n\n## Treasure\n- [ ] Puzzle Piece Tucked in a belt pouch of one of the minions\n- [ ] Caustic Brew x1 (Heals 3d6 HP, but grants the poisoned condition for 3 rounds)\n","x":320,"y":-1180,"width":380,"height":560},
		{"id":"957614cb2efb5516","type":"text","text":"# Skill Challenge\n\n>You see a long corridor in front of you that appears to be broken and battered. you see a number or the floor tiles vibrating with with steam and water seeping from the cracks almost like they are plugging a geyser and pieces of ceiling lying on the floor near the entrance to the room you see a Kobold, lying dead underneath a large stone and I little bit further down the corridor you see another dead Kolbold squished between a floor tile and the ceiling, with a clear note ringing through out the chamber the sound waves appear to be pushing the floor tile against the ceiling. in the Kobold's hand you see something glittering a flash of Jagged Gold. (**Puzzel Piece**) At the far end, you the entrance to what looks to be  a treasury or armory that is obstructed by a fallen pillar. (**Puzzel Piece)\n\n## Encounter\n- [ ] **Resonance Plates** Arcana/Lore DC 12 \n\t- [ ] Failure: 1D6 Damage \n- [ ] Steam Bursts Finesse/Naturecraft DC 12\n\t- [ ] Burned: have disadvantage for the first turn of next check.\n- [ ] Falling Structure: Examinatinon/Finesse\n\t- [ ] 1d6 Damage\n- [ ] Fallen Pillar: Might/Lore DC 12 (Attack 20 hp)\n\t- [ ] alert Sheep Pen Kobolds of your presence -2 init In throne room combat","x":2090,"y":-640,"width":405,"height":840},
		{"id":"775ba94004c9091d","type":"text","text":"# Treasury Antichamber (Dun Vol 1 pg 13 & Vol 2 14)\n> Low-ceilinged stone chamber, reinforced with scavenged masonry\n> \n> Dim torchlight, smoky air, smells of soot, damp stone, and kobolds\n>   \n   Floor cluttered with crates, broken shields, trap components, debris\n  > \n   Acoustics carry scraping and metallic sounds from beyond the walls\n\n### Treasury Access\n- **Ancient Stone Door**\n    - Massive, circular, seamless stone construction\n    - Central **round impression** designed to accept a seal\n    - Worn, barely visible runes radiating outward\n    - Clearly not built by kobolds; old and well-crafted\n- **Child-Sized Hole**\n    - Roughly hacked opening near the door\n    - Claw-scraped stone, uneven, slopes downward\n    - Only Small creatures can traverse easily\n    - Used by kobolds to bypass the sealed door\n## Kobolds Fight \n1. Kobold Den Warden (**Puzzle Piece**)\n\t1. Kobolds x3\n2. Kobold Trapper\n\t1. Kobold Minions X4\n3. Kobold Sneak x2\n\n## Puzzle","x":2600,"y":-1060,"width":405,"height":420},
		{"id":"07f999227759df35","type":"text","text":"# Throne Room (Boss Battle Dun Vol 1 & 2  pg 11)\n- Low-ceilinged stone chamber, reinforced with scavenged masonry\n- Dim torchlight, smoky air, smells of soot, damp stone, and kobolds\n- Floor cluttered with crates, broken shields, trap components, debris\n- Acoustics carry scraping and metallic sounds from beyond the walls\n## Treasure\n- 25 GP per person\n- Snaggletooth's Axe","x":3300,"y":-1060,"width":400,"height":420},
		{"id":"a57e8afba032e2c7","type":"text","text":"# Snaggle Tooth\n## Level 2 Solo monster\nHP: ***75***\nArmor: ***Medium***\nSaves: +STR -INT\n### Actions\n- **Move & Hack***: Move 8, attack for 1d8+2; on Damage **Prone**\n- **Batter Up**: 1d8+2, on damage: they are hit towards another hero within 6 spaces. Both make a DC 12 DEX save or take 1d8+2 damage and re knocked Prone, half damage on save.\n### Bloodied\n@37 HP Snaggel Tooth's Damage increases to 1d12+2\n### Last Stand\nSnaggel Tooth is dying! 20 more damage and he dies. Until then Snaggle Tooth can move **6** spaces and use **Batter UP** each turn.","x":3100,"y":-500,"width":800,"height":650},
		{"id":"4ea121cd21e93e00","type":"text","text":"# Enter the Dungeon \n## Description\n- [ ] Crater Description\n\t- [ ] Yawns before you\n\t- [ ] Glass Scorched Earth\n\t- [ ] Shattered Stone\n\t- [ ] Bottom of the North side of the crater you see what looks to be part of a building made of stone and obsidian.\n\t\t- [ ] Hand carved Stone entrance to a building untouched by Flame or Destruction\n\t\t- [ ] The porch of the structure has 4 columns supporting an awning.\n\t\t- [ ]  Door opened just enough for a child to be able to walk through.\n- [ ] **Lintel** you see an inscription written in an old tongue (DC 12 Lore)\n>Turn Back, keepers of dawn.\n>Within lies the shadow of the unmade sun\n>Touch not the thing that drinks the light.\n>Lest your soul be sung into night.","x":-380,"y":-1180,"width":440,"height":560},
		{"id":"10ac9dee7e45fd02","type":"text","text":"# Quest Hooks\n- **Farmers** are scared of the amount of live stock that has gone missing. They need to conserve their produce to survive the winter.\n- **Treasure** may live inside that Dungeon. Maybe eve powerful magic that will help the community or yourself.\n- **Could we be Next?** Some townsfolk look at the missing live stock as a first fruits of the attacks a head.","x":-640,"y":-40,"width":250,"height":440},
		{"id":"afcfa950f9e47d99","type":"text","text":"# Find the Dungeon\n## Skill challenge\nThere are a number of different clues about who the enemy is and where they are.\n- The farmers found a number of Black Scales in the pastures that had the missing live stock.\n- A majority of the thefts are in the North eastern side of Clackston.\n- **DC 12 Examination/Naturecraft** roll reveals Animal and small clawed Tracks leading to the north\n- **DC 12 Perception** If the Group continues to look around the area they will find a lone Kobold who is trying to pull a stubborn mule in the direction of the gorge. If they capture it, the party can interrogate it. This is a weak will creature that will gladly divulge info about the location of the Warren, and will elude to the \"Big Boss,\" but not give specifics.\n- If they fail both rolls and come up with another solution to find the warren or they just wait to ambush the Thieves next time they come or follow them, they can do that.","x":-1220,"y":-1090,"width":760,"height":380},
		{"id":"2c714c1ee40f6763","type":"text","text":"# Meet with Farmer Glenson\n## Grange Master of the Local Farmer's Grange\n- Meet at the Tavern and wait for further instruction from Master Glenson\n\t- Pose Table: Where the characters meet.\n\t- Character Descriptions and how they present themselves.\n- Meeting taking place in the meeting house\n#### Farmers Affected\n- Master Glenson\n- George Balic\n- Fred Fendroy\n- Patricia Keel\n### Description\n- older man (Salt and Pepper hair)\n- Sitting at the head of the Grange Council table.\n- Crutch sitting close at hand.\n- Lined and leathery skin.\n- darting and piercing eyes that flick to each of you in turn taking in the measure of you.\n### Disposition\n - Short in his speech and strait to the point.\n - Seems irritated that this is happening\n - Man of action, but held fast by his position and an injury to his leg that would only hold a pose back.\n - Want's this finished as soon as possible.\n### Details of the Plan\n - The Thefts are in the North Eastern portion of the \n - The reward is 25 G/person, but he will throw in an extra 5/person if the resolve the problem within a week.","x":-1960,"y":-1219,"width":668,"height":639},
		{"id":"c3dfa5843919bcc6","type":"file","file":"img/Warren's Want/Snaggletooth the Destroyer.png","x":3920,"y":-500,"width":488,"height":650},
		{"id":"a850a2746f503fe3","type":"file","file":"img/Warren's Want/Entrance to the Ring of Battle Barracks.webp","x":-380,"y":-1620,"width":440,"height":440},
		{"id":"06e368426b36ee13","x":320,"y":-1580,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"file","file":"img/Warren's Want/Inside the Ring of Battle Barracks.png"}
	],
